                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Still entertains children so many years later.  I remember fondly watching my late younger brother playing this game, and it does my heart good to watch my daughter do the same.  Hearing her run to me begging me come to see what she found found (an ant tunnel full of ant babiesl) is priceless.\n\nIt's a non-story point and click adventure by Cyan Studios, who also made Manhole, Spelunx and later the Myst games.  The art is simple, but effective, the gameplay is amusing, and it's very good for teaching young children (~3) mouse control. The absurdist comedy really hits home for the young folk, and the focus on cause and effect makes a lasting impression.",
